## Redirection Mapping

Proper 301 redirects are essential to preserve link equity and avoid traffic loss.

Preparation

Estimated time: 10-20 hours

- Crawl current site (Screaming Frog/Ahrefs) to list all URLs.
- Crawl staging/new site for comparison.
- Identify automatically handled redirects (e.g., pattern-based for products/services).

## Create Redirect Map

Estimated time: 40-80 hours (most time-intensive)

- Use 301 permanent redirects for all changed URLs.
- Map 1:1 where possible.
- For removed pages: Redirect to most relevant equivalent (e.g., old loan page new personal lending page). Avoid homepage redirects unless no better option.
- Remove/filter: Duplicates, parameters (?utm=, session IDs), non-indexable files

(unless critical).

## Best Practices for XYZ

- Prioritize high-traffic/backlinked pages (use GA4, GSC, Ahrefs).
- Ensure compliance: Redirects shouldn't mislead users (regulatory consideration).
- Test redirects on staging.

Implementation

Provide map to developers (CSV format: Old URL, New URL, 301). Avoid chains/loops.

Verification

Test with tools like Redirect Checker. Check no blank/missing paths.

## Metadata and Content Transfer

Preserve titles, descriptions, and content to maintain relevance.

## Create Metadata File

Estimated time: 10-20 hours

- Export current titles/descriptions via crawl (Screaming Frog).
- Map to new URLs using VLOOKUP/excel formulas.
- Optimize for E-E-A-T: Include expertise signals, compliance disclaimers.

Transfer Process

Estimated time: 30-70 hours

- Copy/paste or bulk upload optimized metadata.
- Review content for accuracy, trust signals (author bios, sources).
- Ensure schema markup (e.g., FAQ, Organization) transfers.

Template Example

Columns: Old URL, New URL, Title (60 chars max), Description (160 chars), HI, Key Content

